<% content_for :title, "Modal" %>
<div class="mb-8">
  <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Overlays</p>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">Modal</h1>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground">
    A modal a Rails app drives with Turbo: a link asks for a Turbo Stream, the response renders the modal into a container in
    your layout, a frame inside it swaps between show, edit and a 422, and the server closes it with
    <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">turbo_stream.ui_close_modal</code>. It opens as soon as it is rendered, traps focus, locks scroll, asks before
    discarding unsaved form changes, and animates out. Eight positions, from a centred dialog to a side panel or a sheet.
  </p>
</div>

<%# Preview %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Preview</h2>
<div id="modal-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3 p-12 mb-8">
  <% [
    [:center,      "Confirm dialog"],
    [:right,       "Edit panel"],
    [:left,        "Filters"],
    [:top,         "Invite"],
    [:top_full,    "Command palette"],
    [:bottom,      "Share sheet"],
    [:bottom_full, "Action sheet"],
    [:full_screen, "Full screen"],
  ].each do |pos, label| %>
    <%= render(Ui::ButtonComponent.new(href: modal_demo_path(position: pos), variant: :outline, size: :sm,
                                       data: { turbo_stream: true })) { label } %>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%# Usage %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Usage</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  The modal opens as soon as it is rendered. The blessed pattern is a Turbo Stream that renders it
  into a plain container in your layout:
</p>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800 mb-4">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-neutral-900 px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-neutral-400">ERB — layout and trigger</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#modal-trigger" class="text-xs text-neutral-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-neutral-950 px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed"><code id="modal-trigger" class="text-neutral-200"><%= h(example_modal_trigger) %></code></pre>
</div>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800 mb-8">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-neutral-900 px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-neutral-400">ERB — edit.turbo_stream.erb</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#modal-response" class="text-xs text-neutral-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-neutral-950 px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed"><code id="modal-response" class="text-neutral-200"><%= h(example_modal_response) %></code></pre>
</div>

<%# Turbo %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Driving it with Turbo</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  Opening from a stream, swapping an inner content frame, answering an invalid form with a 422,
  closing from the server with <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">turbo_stream.ui_close_modal</code>
  — the whole lifecycle has its own page, with live demos backed by real routes and controller
  actions: <%= link_to "Modal & Turbo", modal_turbo_path, class: "text-primary underline underline-offset-4" %>.
</p>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-8">
  The same guide ships inside the gem at
  <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">docs/guides/modal-and-turbo.md</code>,
  which is where <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">bin/rails g rails_ui_kit:agent_skill</code>
  points this app's coding agents.
</p>

<%# Options %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Options</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-muted">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Name</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Type</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Default</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
      <% [
        ["position",                "Symbol",  ":center", "One of :center, :full_screen, :right, :left, :top, :top_full, :bottom, :bottom_full."],
        ["track_changes",           "Boolean", "false",   "Asks before closing when a form inside is dirty. The form needs data-controller=\"ui--form-change\"."],
        ["close_on_backdrop",       "Boolean", "true",    "Close when the backdrop is clicked. Escape always closes (and asks first when tracking changes)."],
        ["unsaved_changes_title",   "String",  "nil",     "Overrides rails_ui_kit.modal.unsaved_changes_title for this modal."],
        ["unsaved_changes_message", "String",  "nil",     "Overrides rails_ui_kit.modal.unsaved_changes_message for this modal."],
        ["aria",                    "Hash",    "{}",      "Name every modal: { labelledby: \"heading-id\" } for a visible title, or { label: \"…\" } when there is none."],
        ["class",                   "String",  "nil",     "Merged onto the <dialog> with tailwind_merge — a width such as sm:w-[48rem] replaces the position's default."],
      ].each do |name, type, default, desc| %>
        <tr class="hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary"><%= name %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= type %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground"><%= default %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= desc %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<%# Closing %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Closing it</h2>
<ul class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-2 mb-8 list-disc ps-5">
  <li>From the server, after a successful save: <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">&lt;%= turbo_stream.ui_close_modal %&gt;</code> in the stream response.
      It animates the modal out and leaves the container for the next one.</li>
  <li>From a form whose success renders nothing: <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">data-action="turbo:submit-end->ui--modal#closeOnSuccess"</code>
      on the form. An invalid save must answer 422, or this closes on a failure.</li>
  <li>From a button inside it: <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">data-action="click->ui--modal#close"</code>. Escape and the backdrop close it too.</li>
  <li>Before Turbo caches the page, an open modal is removed, so Back never restores one.</li>
</ul>

<%# Accessibility %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Accessibility</h2>
<ul class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-2 mb-8 list-disc ps-5">
  <li>A native modal <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">&lt;dialog&gt;</code> in the top layer: the rest of the page is inert while it's open.</li>
  <li>Focus moves into the modal when it opens and returns to the trigger when it closes — to a trigger with the same id if the
      response that closed it re-rendered the original.</li>
  <li>It has no name of its own. Pass <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria: { labelledby: }</code> pointing at its heading, or <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria: { label: }</code>.</li>
  <li>The unsaved-changes prompt is the kit's confirm dialog, so it is keyboard-operable and announced like any dialog.</li>
</ul>

<%# Not this %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">When not to use it</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-8">
  Don't render it inline in a page: it opens on every page load. A yes/no question before an action is a
  <%= link_to "Confirm Dialog", confirm_dialog_path, class: "text-primary underline" %>, usually through <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">data-turbo-confirm</code>.
  Content anchored to a control that doesn't block the page is a <%= link_to "Popover", popover_path, class: "text-primary underline" %>.
  And a task long enough to deserve its own URL — something people bookmark, share or return to — is a page.
</p>
